TRANSCRIBED MATERIAL — READ THIS BEFORE REUSING
===============================================================================

These harnesses exist to MEASURE, not to compute correctly. Each one transcribes
an algorithm's arithmetic from a reference implementation so that Vivado can be
asked what it costs in LUTs, FFs, DSPs, BRAM and achievable clock. Every source
file says so in its header, and says what was and was not verified. That warning
is the most important thing in this repository:

    "NOT VERIFIED against the reference. Area and timing only."

**Do not lift this RTL into a miner.** It produces numbers Vivado can measure,
not hashes a chain will accept.

The upstream sources, and their licences as reported by the GitHub API on
2026-09-28:

Odocrypt — DigiByte
  github.com/DigiByte-Core/digibyte — MIT
  rtl/odo_round.sv transcribes one round from src/crypto/odocrypt.cpp
  (ApplyPbox, ApplySboxes, ApplyRotations, ApplyRoundKey). The algorithm's own
  header states the design intent that the 6-bit S-boxes suit FPGA logic
  elements and the 10-bit ones FPGA RAM, which is what made it worth measuring.

XelisHash v3 — Xelis
  github.com/xelis-project/xelis-hash — MIT
  rtl/xelis_pkg.sv transcribes constants from src/v3.rs, pinned at sha256
  ee9c746ef9765b9efa7bca3670c2a6ca380ba8fcc9ce4a376704d022bcd34254.
  rtl/xelis_branch_alu.sv transcribes all 16 data-selected branch cases.
  xelis_isqrt in rtl/xelis_prims.sv reproduces the reference's OVERFLOW
  behaviour deliberately, including the two saturating cases — the only part of
  this repository that was verified against the reference, by tb/verify_isqrt.py.

Poseidon2 over Goldilocks — Quantus
  github.com/Quantus-Network/qp-poseidon — MIT
  rtl/gl_pkg.sv and rtl/gl_prims.sv transcribe the Goldilocks field helpers
  (p = 2^64 - 2^32 + 1) and the Poseidon2 permutation from src/goldilocks.rs
  and src/poseidon2.rs. gl_pkg.sv notes that reduce128 is transcribed line for
  line, which is the closest thing here to copied expression rather than
  reimplemented arithmetic — hence this attribution.

All three upstreams are MIT, which is compatible with this repository's MIT and
requires attribution; that is what this file provides. **The licences were
checked on 2026-09-28 and upstream terms can change.** Re-check before
redistributing, and note the Quantus chain was roughly two weeks old when it was
screened, so its repository is more likely than the others to have moved.

===============================================================================
GENERATED FILES
===============================================================================

odocrypt-ooc/rtl/odo_tables.svh is generated by gen_tables.py, not written. It
is committed anyway so the measurement is reproducible without running Python:
the generator seeds a fixed RNG (0xD16B17E), so regenerating reproduces it
byte for byte. The table CONTENTS are not what was being measured — their shape
is — but they must be random permutations, because structured tables let
synthesis optimise away work a real epoch would demand.
